.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd June 9, 2026
.Dt EMACS-JOURNAL-2026-06-09 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-journal-2026-06-09
.Nd working notes of 2026-06-09
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss Fix jotain.service daemon crash (exit 255) + make package fetching optional
.Ss Summary
The
.Ql "jotain.service"
systemd user unit on an offline host was in a restart loop, exiting
.Ql "255/EXCEPTION"
on every start.
The journal showed failing MELPA/NonGNU archive downloads, which \fIlooked\fP like the cause but are caught and non-fatal.
The real fatal error was
.Ql "tagref-mode" .
.Ss Root cause
.Ql "init-prog.el"
hooked
.Ql "tagref-mode"
onto \fBevery\fP
.Ql "prog-mode"
buffer unconditionally.
.Ql "tagref.el"
.No \&( Ns Ql "tagref-mode" )
calls
.Ql "(user-error \(dqNot in a project; tagref-mode requires project.el\(dq)"
when there is no project.
During daemon startup
.Ql "*scratch*"
is created in
.Ql "lisp-interaction-mode"
(a
.Ql "prog-mode"
descendant); with the unit's
.Ql "default-directory"
=
.Ql "$HOME"
(not a project) the hook fired and signalled.
This happens in
.Ql "command-line"
\fBbefore\fP
.Ql "--fg-daemon" Ns No "'s"
.Ql "server-start" Ns No "/sd_notify,"
so the daemon died un-notified → systemd reported
.Ql "255/EXCEPTION" .
.Pp
Confirmed by the journal ordering:
.Ql "\(dqNot in a project; tagref-mode requires project.el\(dq"
→
.Ql "\(dqWrote …/var/recentf-save.el\(dq"
(only runs from
.Ql "kill-emacs-hook" )
→ exit 255.
.Ql "init.el"
had fully loaded, so the MELPA failures never aborted startup.
Dev machines hid the bug: their daemon usually starts inside the repo (a project), where
.Ql "tagref-mode"
enables cleanly.
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "lisp/init-prog.el" Ns No "\fP"
—
.Ql "tagref"
.Ql "use-package"
block: replaced
.Ql ":hook (prog-mode . tagref-mode)"
with
.Ql ":hook (prog-mode . jotain-tagref--maybe-enable)" ,
a guard (defined in
.Ql ":init" ,
with
.Ql ":commands (tagref-mode)"
for the autoload) that enables
.Ql "tagref-mode"
only when
.Ql "(project-current)"
is non-nil.
Outside a project it declines silently instead of signalling.
This is the crash fix.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "init.el" Ns No "\fP"
— reworked archive fetching to be optional, background, and non-fatal (per request):
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
New
.Ql "jotain-refresh-package-archives"
defvar, defaulting off when the
.Ql "JOTAIN_NO_PACKAGE_REFRESH"
env var is set — the per-host opt-out for offline machines, no shared-config edit needed.
.It
On-demand refresh advice now removes itself \fIbefore\fP refreshing and wraps
.Ql "package-refresh-contents"
in
.Ql "with-demoted-errors" ,
so a dead network is a log line, not a fatal error, and can't re-trigger on every later install.
.It
Added a background warm-up on
.Ql "emacs-startup-hook"
via
.Ql "run-with-idle-timer"
using async
.Ql "(package-refresh-contents t)" ,
also demoted — never blocks the daemon, never fails the service.
.El
.El
.Ss Follow-up for the offline host
Optional: set
.Ql "Environment=JOTAIN_NO_PACKAGE_REFRESH=1"
on the
.Ql "jotain.service"
unit (or via
.Ql "services.jotain" )
to silence the now-harmless download-failure log lines.
Not changed in the shared default.
.Ss Silence the corfu/ispell completion-at-point error storm
.Ss Summary
.Ql "*Messages*"
was flooded with
.Ql "Corfu detected an error: … ispell-lookup-words: No plain word-list found at system default locations"
backtraces, one per keystroke in any
.No "text/YAML/Markdown/" Ns Ql "COMMIT_EDITMSG"
buffer.
Corfu catches the error, but it spams the log and silently disables in-buffer completion there.
.Ss Root cause
Emacs 30 added the
.Ql "text-mode-ispell-word-completion"
option, which \fBdefaults to
.Ql "completion-at-point" Ns No "\fP."
With that default,
.Ql "text-mode"
adds
.Ql "ispell-completion-at-point"
to
.Ql "completion-at-point-functions"
in every text-mode-derived buffer.
.Ql "ispell-completion-at-point"
→
.Ql "ispell-lookup-words"
reads
.Ql "ispell-alternate-dictionary" ,
whose default is
.Ql "/usr/share/dict/words"
— \fBabsent on NixOS\fP, so every corfu auto-completion in a prose buffer throws.
We spell-check with jinx, so the ispell capf is pure breakage here.
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "lisp/init-writing.el" Ns No "\fP"
— added
.Ql "(text-mode-ispell-word-completion nil)"
to the
.Ql "text-mode"
.Ql "use-package"
.Ql ":custom"
block, with a comment explaining the NixOS word-list gap.
Verified: with the option nil,
.Ql "ispell-completion-at-point"
is no longer present in a text-mode buffer's
.Ql "completion-at-point-functions" .
.El
.Ss Not changed (separate, deployment-dependent)
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "Jinx: No dictionaries available for \(dqen_US\(dq" Ns No "\fP"
— enchant has no en_US dictionary backend on this host (no
.Ql "enchant" Ns No "/dict"
on PATH).
Fix belongs at the deployment layer (provide a hunspell/nuspell en_US dict +
.Ql "DICPATH" ,
or switch the daily Emacs to the Nix-wrapped
.Ql "jotainEmacsPackages"
and add the dict there).
Left for a follow-up once the daily-Emacs deployment path is confirmed.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "Failed to download 'melpa'/'melpa-stable' archive" Ns No "\fP"
— the same transient, non-fatal background archive warm covered above; not a regression.
.El
.Ss Drop withJansson from emacs.nix (nixpkgs make-emacs.nix removed it)
.Ss Summary
.Ql "nix flake check --all-systems"
failed during package evaluation with
.Ql "function 'anonymous lambda' called with unexpected argument 'withJansson'"
pointing at nixpkgs'
.Ql "make-emacs.nix" .
Surfaced after the in-progress flake update (nixpkgs →
.Ql "8c3cede7" ,
emacs-overlay →
.Ql "2aba9beb" ).
.Ss Root cause
Upstream nixpkgs removed the
.Ql "withJansson"
argument from
.Ql "pkgs/applications/editors/emacs/make-emacs.nix"
— Emacs 30+ has built-in JSON, so the
.Ql "--with-jansson"
flag is gone.
.Ql "emacs.nix"
still declared
.Ql "withJansson ? false"
and forwarded it through
.Ql "basePackage.override" ,
so the override threw on the now-unknown argument.
Confirmed
.Ql "withJansson"
is absent from the pinned
.Ql "make-emacs.nix"
formal argument list; every other flag we forward is still accepted.
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "emacs.nix" Ns No "\fP"
— removed the
.Ql "withJansson ? false"
parameter and its entry in the
.Ql "basePackage.override"
.Ql "inherit"
block.
No other forwarded flag changed.
.El
.Ss Verification
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Cache-parity invariant still holds:
.Ql "(import ./emacs.nix {}).outPath == pkgs.emacs-git.outPath"
evaluates to
.Ql "true" ,
so the mainline build remains a binary-cache hit.
.It
Committed alongside the nixpkgs/emacs-overlay bump that triggered it;
.Ql "just verify"
confirms
.Ql "flake.lock"
and
.Ql "devenv.lock"
agree on all shared inputs.
.El
